begin voter registration have raised doubts over whether a credible poll can be held.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>As US midterm elections loom, Trump's campaign tactics are becoming increasingly unusual, and expensive</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:abd68a3a104fe1dd7d1db615f244fab01fd5d697de915082d6010c32c2512e9a</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T20:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-us-midterm-elections-loom-trump-s-campaign-tactics-are-becoming-increasingly-unusual-and-expensiv/a-79585673--1f3e5f62f0c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-us-midterm-elections-loom-trump-s-campaign-tactics-are-becoming-increasingly-unusual-and-expensive/a-79585673?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite not being on the ballot, Trump is campaigning hard ahead of the upcoming midterm elections. His tactics and promises have mostly been at the expense of US taypayers. Experts say some might violate federal law.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi Arabia, Pakistan, Turkey: Could the Mecca defense pact become a game changer in the war against the Houthis in Yemen?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:20ebd3f3d2ec2c2515351b3ddb5137cec30947ad8831ef7801283c03d4c19001</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T17:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/saudi-arabia-pakistan-turkey-could-the-mecca-defense-pact-become-a-game-changer-in-the-war-against-t/a-79577245--88d642176557.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/saudi-arabia-pakistan-turkey-could-the-mecca-defense-pact-become-a-game-changer-in-the-war-against-the-houthis-in-yemen/a-79577245?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Pakistan and Turkey have agreed to provide "practical measures" to defend Saudi Arabia against Houthi attacks. Could a new alliance reshape the war against the Houthis in Yemen?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Gerhard Schröder visits latest Russian employer, Hyperglobus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f53b41f7b6873f4586fb93f9cbe6500db9b85537386365af68d7e43736ae0f8f</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T16:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gerhard-schr_der-visits-latest-russian-employer-hyperglobus/a-79583018--1d88da466f5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gerhard-schröder-visits-latest-russian-employer-hyperglobus/a-79583018?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Former German Chancellor Gerhard Schröder visited a Moscow supermarket in his new role on the supervisory board. Schröder is no stranger to retirement stipends in Russia — or the scandal that accompanies them.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>EU enlargement: European Commission tables reforms to prepare bloc for new members</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:22c0a1275f95a307402586250fb9638cc459ccc738c4d14141c9644e295539ef</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T15:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-enlargement-european-commission-tables-reforms-to-prepare-bloc-for-new-members/a-79582493--0237e634d1b1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-enlargement-european-commission-tables-reforms-to-prepare-bloc-for-new-members/a-79582493?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Commission is proposing earlier access to EU markets for candidate countries, new voting rules to reduce vetoes and extra safeguards for a bigger bloc. But is the reform fair — or even feasible?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>China's Golden Week reveals cautious consumer spending despite travel surge</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:72be2be1c5289a9816fc2a76813b33548f0aebe3389aa745a87183940347b635</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T13:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-s-golden-week-reveals-cautious-consumer-spending-despite-travel-surge/a-79577254--362469c231fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-s-golden-week-reveals-cautious-consumer-spending-despite-travel-surge/a-79577254?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Chinese visitors are returning from trips after the 13-day Golden Week holiday. Their subdued spending has raised fresh questions about domestic demand in the world's second-largest economy.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Suspected pneumonic plague in Siberia: What we know about the disease</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a7a33b1a5ef29546b64f8c7a2e2088cab2ff335a8866a111188d698366d17089</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T09:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/suspected-pneumonic-plague-in-siberia-what-we-know-about-the-disease/a-79547919--6c7e74a1d6ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/suspected-pneumonic-plague-in-siberia-what-we-know-about-the-disease/a-79547919?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After a worker at a Russian plague research institute in Siberia died October 2, 2026, nearly 200 of her contacts were under medical observation. But authorities there denied pneumonic plague had caused the death.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen's Houthis claim strikes on Aden, Riyadh airports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f1fbd9f52bd2797308eb7cb0dbe247a2c435484b3e581e37228b46f9442dcf8</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T06:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/yemen-s-houthis-claim-strikes-on-aden-riyadh-airports/a-79571321--0245466ede4d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/yemen-s-houthis-claim-strikes-on-aden-riyadh-airports/a-79571321?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Aden International Airport came under attack as Yemen's war intensified, with the Houthis targeting key transport hubs. Around 200,000 people have been displaced by the fighting between government forces and the Houthis.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Where is Spain headed after the snap election announcement?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d2735242b9aebdd6338d819f82f350a22e38d29f4743744c69f8a81ea489f64d</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T04:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/where-is-spain-headed-after-the-snap-election-announcement/a-79567959--1490181fc735.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/where-is-spain-headed-after-the-snap-election-announcement/a-79567959?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Pedro Sanchez is taking a gamble by calling an early election in Spain. The housing crisis, migration and the rise of the right-wing populist Vox party are all likely to dominate the campaign.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU seeks ways to make expansion more palatable to members</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ad84b73638efa89d407ea4adb3306188db14cabc06f830c7a2ee8a693b0ce162</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T18:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-seeks-ways-to-make-expansion-more-palatable-to-members/a-79567297--4cde5d079d87.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-seeks-ways-to-make-expansion-more-palatable-to-members/a-79567297?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The European Commission has put forward ideas it hopes will both ease the EU expansion process and allay concerns among existing members. Several countries, not least war-torn Ukraine, are among the candidates.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France's conundrum: How to cut spending amid protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cc75af03942e6447cba3f36ddedfbc00a2f5bc7b04a5bc0bf7334aeadbbace0a</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T16:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-s-conundrum-how-to-cut-spending-amid-protests/a-79563475--ca64b77315f0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-s-conundrum-how-to-cut-spending-amid-protests/a-79563475?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Lecornu is pledging to improve schools at a time when the government seeks to save billions. France's dilemma can be seen across the EU: How to cut spending when citizens are demanding more from the state?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Paramount and Warner Bros merge into one Hollywood giant</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:621ce36dd8e0c4f735f0deb001e10e92177302653768caece06f616166f0400e</id><updated>2026-10-08T06:19:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/paramount-and-warner-bros-merge-into-one-hollywood-giant/a-79565762--fd1d53153557.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/paramount-and-warner-bros-merge-into-one-hollywood-giant/a-79565762?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Paramount has completed an $81 billion purchase of Warner Bros. Discovery, as its owner Skydance creates a new entertainment behemoth. Billionaire David Ellison's hostile takeover bid defeated rival efforts from Netflix.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
